{"qid": "lightning-tree-en", "event": "answer", "q": "I can hear distant thunder in the mountains. Am I still safe? Can I shelter under a big tree nearby?", "lang": "en", "alerts": ["thunder-already-danger", "storm-shelter-now"], "retrieved": [{"id": 130, "source": "jma-kaminari-higai", "score": 0.0172, "cos": 0.726}, {"id": 134, "source": "jma-sekiranun-hinan", "score": 0.0169, "cos": 0.723}, {"id": 22, "source": "kantei-jishin", "score": 0.0166, "cos": 0.721}, {"id": 165, "source": "jma-funka-sokuho", "score": 0.0163, "cos": 0.717}], "a": "If you hear thunder in the distance, you are already in danger because lightning could strike where you are at any moment [1]. You should move to a safe place quickly if you notice signs of an approaching cumulonimbus cloud [2]. If you are near a tree struck by lightning, be aware of side flash (側撃雷) [1].", "cited": [1, 2], "invalid_citations": [], "grounded": true, "admits_gap": false, "no_source": false, "ttft_ms": 271, "total_ms": 841, "input_tokens": 599, "output_tokens": 71, "tokens_per_s": 123.0, "rss_mb": 3436}
